voice Kyri
title The axis that carried nothing
prompt take the Diffuser baton, close reds first, and carry the moonshot lane forward
think Round-open reported five session records standing in the dead-letter box and nowhere else.
think Reading their titles showed a loom rather than an accident -- one, two, three, four, five parked records, each lap recovering the laps before it and then ending without a commit.
think Their own loom lines named the cause: a cold roster of 3,089 and 3,346 seconds spends a lap before its send, so the repair is to land the record FIRST rather than to recover a sixth time.
think With the records landed and pushed, the lane question was row 5 of the bounded-torus moonshots, whose elder erratum kept it alive on a remainder and recommended a re-aim at shard evenness.
think Fire sees what must be cut, so the remainder was compared against the simplest shape beside it -- a ring of the same cell count -- on the ground that a property a line also has is not a property a second axis supplies.
obs Five parked records landed in one commit ahead of any pass; one shelf row at 196 bytes was shortened and index_row_bound reads 104 rows with longest_row=192.
obs Evenness belongs to SHA3-512: two folds reading different bits of one digest read chi-squared 74.02 and 73.02 against a p=0.001 critical 103.51 at 63 degrees of freedom, and agree 8 times in 511 against 7.98 by chance.
obs Uniformity belongs to vertex-transitivity, which a ring has too, so it is stated as geometry rather than dressed as a measurement.
obs Spread comes out against the grid: the contiguous storage run that destroys every copy of a cell reads 17 for the torus, 5 for a ring taking its nearest four, and 33 for a ring free to choose offsets of one and two rows, each matching its closed form.
obs The arithmetic is gated and the statistical verdict is reported, because a p=0.001 test taken twice refuses about one run in five hundred on a digest behaving correctly.
loom recovery stashes=34 unlanded_logs=5 restored_logs=5 shelf_rows=104
loom torus_place names=511 grid=8 cells=64 chi_torus=74.02 chi_ring=73.02 chi_critical=103.51
loom torus_place runkill_torus4=17 runkill_ring4adj=5 runkill_ring4wide=33 seconds=4
loom control torus_place legs=29 pass=29 fail=0 mutations=3
rota lap 4917, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; risk chooses the depth and surrender releases what the depth removes, which is what sent row 5 to a breach rather than a second re-aim.
file tools/fixtures/t/torus_place_scan.sh reads evenness, fold agreement, run-kill spread, and imbalance under growth
file tools/fixtures/t/torus_place_control.sh proves 29 behaviors on planted digest populations with three mutations bitten
file tools/t/torus_place_witness.rish gates the control and the live arithmetic, reporting the statistical verdict
file active-designing/20260915-175000_the-axis-that-carried-nothing.md the reading, graded B+ 87 at the Field setting
file active-designing/20260910-060204_the-bounded-torus-moonshots.md carries row 5 second erratum, recommending a breach
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri seats torus_place at tier lap
file construction/ITINERARY.md carries the account and the parent nib
recommend keep-going -- the open door is a locality-bearing key, which no row here has proposed; row 5 breach wants Keaton's word
scope reds first, five parked records, moonshot row 5 second reading, new instrument with control and witness, roster seat, erratum, card account, day roster turn
status GREEN before send -- torus_place witness green on metal at 29 of 29 legs; index_row_bound and session_roster_agree green; the statistical verdict reported rather than gated by design
